<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="to_open_an_app_940c6a" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>To open an app</title>
   <shortdesc>The My Apps check box is an App designer option only for testing apps.</shortdesc>
   <prolog>
      <author type="creator">Rakesh Singh</author>
      <critdates>
         <revised modified="Jan 30, 2019"/>
      </critdates>
       <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>click</keyword>
        <keyword>Apps</keyword>
        <keyword>placeholder</keyword>
        <keyword>Application</keyword>
        <keyword>Search</keyword>
        <keyword>Excel</keyword>
        <indexterm>click</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Apps</indexterm>
        <indexterm>placeholder</indexterm>
      </keywords>
          <prodinfo>
        <prodname/>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <taskbody>
      <steps>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click <b>Apps</b> and then click Open Application to view the available Apps to open.</cmd>
            <info>
               <image href="../attachments/98667731/98667980.png" width="46" height="91" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Either scroll down to find an App or enter in the App name in Search by Application Name and click <b>Search</b>. Then either double-click on the App or click <b>Select</b>.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98667979</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667731/98667979.png" width="608" height="297" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
            <info>
               <note type="note">
                  <p>The My Apps check box is an App designer option only for testing apps.</p>
               </note>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>You can also select an App from the shortcut list.</cmd>
         </step>
      </steps>
      <result>
         <fig>
            <title>98667978</title>
            <image href="../attachments/98667731/98667978.png" width="249" height="134" placement="break">
               <alt>placeholder</alt>
            </image>
         </fig>
         <p>After the App loads into Excel, you will see custom menus created specifically for the chosen app, such as Retrieve Opportunities, as well as one or more of the X-Author for Excel standard buttons: Add Row, Paste, Delete Row(s) from your environment.</p>
      </result>
   </taskbody>
</task>